        "job_name": "SIGNAL LOST",
        "job_description": "An oddity. ==The Diable Avionics Corporation is paying for the destruction of a fleet flying its own colors.==\n\nA DSF carrier group on extended recon picked up a burst of ==pre-Collapse Corporation ID codes== from beyond the explored Sector. They traced the signal to a fleet, followed it into a…REDACTED, and made first contact.\n\nIn a rare display of candor or a routine exercise in calculation, the Admiralty has attached the few seconds of blurry footage a recon Vapor managed to transmit. You’re being asked for a second opinion.\n\n// …CONTROL! THEY’RE NOT FRIENDLY! THEY’RE NOT—\n[STATIC]\n…LOST THE WHOLE… OH GOD. I CAN’T GET THE HARNESS OFF.\n…CONTROL, PLEASE. SEND… SEND THE LAST LI—\n[SIGNAL LOST] //\n\nThe clip cuts to static, then starts again. The screams and creaks meld into one, like listening to the wails of dying animals through an analog interface.\n\nEven through the blur, the battle-worn ships move and coordinate in an organic, almost rehearsed manner as they slaughter the Admiralty’s carrier group. You look for the Wanzers and spot only a couple of sixth-generation antiques. ==The Cruiser School==, honed for a single purpose. From the look of it, that purpose was to dismantle their own faction.\n\nYour XO looks away after the third replay.\n\nThe bounty is substantial. The pre-Collapse hardware could be worth a fortune on its own, assuming you’re the one picking through the wreckage.",
        "job_intel_success": "Diable confirms the destruction of the flagship and releases your payment. The final receipt lists the ship as unidentified.",
        "job_intel_failure": "Diable has verified that the flagship is in your possession. The Corporation closes the contract without payment.",
